# probe-06 minmax_decline_missed_stats
# GAP: MIN/MAX are not foldable in the fused aggregate (resolve_agg_folds :1785 returns
#   None for anything but Count/Sum/Avg) -> generic aggregate pipeline over a FULL scan.
#   This is a DOUBLE miss: MIN/MAX of a scalar column are answerable directly from Iceberg
#   column min/max stats (same stats the file-pruner already reads, stat_bounds :317-374),
#   so a manifest/stats shortcut analogous to PR-1's COUNT(*) is left on the table.
# MECHANISM that SHOULD (ideally) fire: a MIN/MAX-from-column-stats shortcut. None today.
# PREDICTED: files_selected>0, full FACT_ORDER decode of ORDER_TOTAL, seconds-class cold —
#   despite the answer being derivable without reading a single data file.
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT (MIN(?tot) AS ?lo) (MAX(?tot) AS ?hi)
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:orderTotal ?tot . }
